  so that gives us 720 so that's the sum  of all the interior angles but then  we're dividing by the sixth interior  angles so 720 divided by 6 equals 120  thinking we got here so sometimes it's  easier to use this formula and then just  subtract from 180 to find the interior  angle just a little bit quicker for  number three now what do you think for  this one well it looks like we're given  the exterior angles here and we know  that all those exterior angles add up to  360 now this is not a regular polygon  all the sides and all the angles are not  the same but they always add up to 360  so let's just make an equation here 90  plus 90 is 180 plus 150 is 330 plus x  equals 360 degrees so if we subtract 330  from both sides you can see that ax this  missing angle here would be a 30 degree  angle okay number four five and six  these are like word problems see if you  can do these on your own and we'll go  through them number four says name the  regular polygon with interior angles  that sum to two thousand eight hundred  and eighty degrees okay so basically  they're telling us all those angles on  the inside of the polygon add up to 2880  so we want to use this formula right  here it's going to be n minus two times  180 equals the total the interior angles  which they tell us is two thousand eight  hundred and eighty degrees so you can do  this a couple different ways you could  distribute the 180 like this or you can  divide both sides by 180  I'll just distribute so this is 180 n  minus 360 equals two thousand eight  hundred and eighty if we add 360 to both  sides that gives us a hundred and eighty  n equals let's do this on the calculator  to eight eight zero plus 360 so that's  32 40 and if we divide both sides by 180  that comes out to 18 so that means this  is an 18 gone okay meaning it has 18  angles or 18 sides and it's a regular 18  guy okay for number five now it says  mean the regular polygon so another  regular one that has an exterior angle  of 30 degrees okay so let's use this  formula over here if we want to find  them  just one exterior angle it comes out to  360 divided by n equals the measure of  that exterior angle which in this case  they tell us is 30 degrees so what we  can do here is we can think of this as  30 over 1 and we can cross multiply on  the diagonal so this is the cross  product property so 30 times N equals  360 times 1 which is 360 and if we  divide both sides by 30 n comes out to  12 so you could say this is a 12 God or  this is also called a dodecagon okay  dodecagon decagon is 10 sides dodecagon  12 and then number 6 here it says name  the regular polygon that has an interior  angle of 170 now sometimes I like to  change up the problem a little bit like  if we know the interior angle is 170 how  much is the exterior angle well just  like we were talking about in a previous  problem they're supplementary the  interior angle the exterior angle which  means that the exterior angle would be  10 and we can use this formula just like  we did in this last problem but in this  case I'm going to use this formula right  here the measure of an interior angle so  it's n minus 2 times 180 divided by the  number of interior angles equals the  measure of one of those interior angles  now what we can do is we can also do the  cross product so 170 N equals 180 times  n minus 2 because anything times 1 is  itself let's distribute the 180 so that  comes out to 180 and minus 360 equals  170 N let's subtract the 180 n that will  give us negative 10 N equals negative  360 and if we divide by negative 10 and  comes out to 36 so that means that this  is a 36 God meaning has 36 sides or 36  angles if you want to see more examples  follow me over to that video right there  where we dive into some more examples  similar these so you can get some more  practice I'll see over in that video

